      "sourceHash": "5eb6cf647d2c5d14a044e2d103dcef4cf0cdc872434c374debc1043092bc4746",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "api_symbol",
      "contextBefore": "[Creating auxiliary depth data manually](creating-auxiliary-depth-data-manually.md)",
      "contextAfter": "When using `CGImageSource` functions to read from a HEIF, JPEG, or DNG file containing depth data (as well as image data), you can use the [`CGImageSourceCopyAuxiliaryDataInfoAtIndex(_:_:_:)`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/ImageIO/CGImageSourceCopyAuxiliaryDataInfoAtIndex(_:_:_:)) function to load primitive depth map information, then use this initializer to create an [`AVDepthData`](avdepthdata.md) object, as shown below.",
